  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SBGs Improving access to income-generating opportunities and schools rehabilitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1 200 youth (at least 50% female; and 20 PWDs) improved their personal and professional capacity and increased their employability through relevant skills training in Idleb and Aleppo.&#xA0;
Output 1.2 134 best proposals (individual or group submissions) have received small livelihood activation grants to enable them to start their own business in Idlib and Aleppo. Grants will be on average 2500 USD based on Violet&apos;s past experience in the context during the implementation of different similar projects, also this is harmonized with ERL cluster and the joint BSP technical work group under FSL, ERL and CWG
Output 1.3&#xA0;30 schools in four districts (Ariha, Harim, Idleb, and Jisr Al-Shughur) in Idleb governorate are rehabilitated.</narrative>
  </description>
